#---
# purpose: "a message no parked receive matches is gifted whole and waits in the receiver's mailbox until a later receive asks for it; the receiver's heap allocates nothing for either delivery"
#---
#
# The parent parks on `:go`. The child's first send, `{:other, [7, 8]}`, is
# rejected by the matcher, so the child gifts the whole message and the parent
# stays parked. The second send, `:go`, matches and wakes the parent. The parent
# grafts both gifts at its dispatch: `:go` finishes the first receive and
# `{:other, [7, 8]}` is in the mailbox for the second. Both lists the parent
# prints were allocated by the child; the parent's own `list_cons_allocs` does
# not move.
def main() do
  parent = self()
  spawn(fn () ->
    send(parent, {:other, [7, 8]})
    send(parent, :go)
  end)
  before = Process.heap_alloc_stats()
  receive do
    :go -> dbg(:go)
  end
  receive do
    {:other, xs} -> dbg(xs)
  end
  after_receive = Process.heap_alloc_stats()
  dbg(after_receive[:list_cons_allocs] - before[:list_cons_allocs])
end
